      "created_at": "2014-07-22T10:20:39Z",
      "updated_at": "2014-07-22T10:20:39Z",
      "body": "It is possible to crash Python by breaking opened gdbm database.\r\n\r\n```pycon\n>>> import _gdbm as dbm\r\n>>> db = dbm.open('x.db', 'n')\r\n>>> open('x.db', 'wb').close()\r\n>>> db[b'a'] = b'b'\r\ngdbm fatal: read error\n```\n\r\n\r\nProposed patch tries to convert fatal gdbm into regular exception or in Python fatal error (which at least produces traceback).\r\n\r\n```pycon\n>>> import _gdbm as dbm\r\n>>> db = dbm.open('x.db', 'n')\r\n>>> open('x.db', 'wb').close()\r\n>>> db[b'a'] = b'b'\r\nTraceback (most recent call last):\r\n  File \"<stdin>\", line 1, in <module>\r\n_gdbm.error: gdbm fatal: read error\n```",
      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "pin": null,
