      "updated_at": "2025-05-25T15:50:08Z",
      "body": "The issue still exists; I can reproduce it on Python 3.15\n```python\n$ ./python\nPython 3.15.0a0 (heads/main:91b48868a8, May 25 2025, 18:45:04) [GCC 15.1.1 20250425] on linux\nType \"help\", \"copyright\", \"credits\" or \"license\" for more information.\n>>> import _gdbm as dbm\n>>> db = dbm.open('x.db', 'n')\n>>> open('x.db', 'wb').close()\n>>> db[b'a'] = b'b'\n[1]    163083 bus error (core dumped)  ./python\n```",
